{
  "_comment": "Who someone is: rolled once from their people's template (Dwarf Fortress style). Every range is 7 breakpoints: the six gaps between them are equally likely and a value is uniform inside its gap, so spacing the numbers shapes the odds. Attributes run 0-5000 (1000 = an ordinary human); facets 0-100 (50 = ordinary); values -50..50. Texts are chosen by band, so the words always match the numbers: attributes and features by the gap their roll fell in, facets 0-9 / 10-24 / 76-90 / 91-100, values 26+ or -26 or less. A race lists only what differs from 'default'.",

  "attributes": ["Strength", "Agility", "Toughness", "Endurance", "Recuperation", "DiseaseResistance",
